---
/**
 * About.
 *
 * The one page whose job is the through-line: paramedic, then construction,
 * then AI. Every claim here is on /cv. Nothing is invented, and the prose is
 * deliberately plain — see the note at the bottom of this file.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Youniss Kandah: paramedic, then construction, then AI. Why emergency systems and construction documents are not unfamiliar territory."
>
  <div class="page-narrow">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="About"
      title="About"
      description="I'm an AI engineer at ONDEWO, working on AI4Emergency. Before I wrote software for a field, I worked in the field."
      meta={['Last updated: 2026-08']}
    />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="label">Health care</h2>
        <p class="meta">Samariterbund · 9 months</p>
      </div>

      <p class="max-w-text text-ink-muted">
        I worked as a paramedic at Samariterbund for nine months. Emergency response, patients in
        front of me, and a job where the time something takes is part of whether it works.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="label">Construction</h2>
        <p class="meta">HTL Mödling · ib-data / ABK</p>
      </div>

      <p class="max-w-text text-ink-muted">
        I spent five years at HTL Mödling on the construction track, then three years at ib-data
        building software for construction management. Semantic search over specifications,
        PDF and Excel sources turned into structured data, a customer portal, a detection model
        for doors and windows in drawings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="label">Artificial intelligence</h2>
        <p class="meta">JKU Linz · ONDEWO</p>
      </div>

      <p class="max-w-text text-ink-muted">
        I did my BSc in Artificial Intelligence at JKU Linz and finished ahead of the standard
        duration, with a thesis on deep learning for language-based audio retrieval. I now work at
        ONDEWO on retrieval, evaluation and agent infrastructure in Python.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="label">What it means for the work</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="max-w-text text-ink-muted">
        AI4Emergency is AI for emergency communication, and I have worked in emergency response.
        The document work at ib-data was construction documents, and I was trained in construction
        before that. In both cases I knew what the documents were for and who was reading them
        before I started building.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 max-w-text text-ink-muted">
        That does not make a model more accurate on its own. It does mean I can usually tell when
        an output is wrong.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="label">Elsewhere on this site</h2>
      </div>

      <p class="max-w-text text-ink-muted">
        The detail is in <a class="link" href="/work/">Work</a> and
        <a class="link" href="/projects/">Projects</a>, and the short version is on the
        <a class="link" href="/cv/">CV</a>. To reach me, use the
        <a class="link" href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

